  "broader": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/he-c/6916",
  "definition": "Staff-to-Child Ratio and Group Size",
  "effectiveDate": "2023-05-25",
  "historyNote": "#12536, eff 5-24-18; ss by #13650, eff 5-25-23",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "He-C 6916.15",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-c6900.html",
  "prefLabel": "He-C 6916.15 Staff-to-Child Ratio and Group Size",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-C 6916.15 Staff-to-Child Ratio and Group Size.\n\n(a) The staff-to-child ratio for school-age programs shall be one staff for 15 children with a maximum group size of 60.\n\n(b) In addition to the staffing requirements in (a) above, programs shall have a second staff person in the building when 13 or more children are present.\n\n(c) Programs shall provide a minimum of 40 square feet of usable indoor space per child. Indoor active play space shall be available to children daily.\n\n(d) In addition to (a) above, programs offering drop-in care shall monitor attendance records to ensure compliance with group size and ratios. If there is a pattern of exceeding ratio and group size then additional staff shall be added. Attendance records shall be kept on file for 6 months for review by the department.\n\n(e) The only exception to (a) above shall be when children combine for time-limited activities, such as meals, snacks, daily meetings, short stories, special guest presentations, or other special events, provided that all children have sufficient space for the activity.\n\nSource. #12536, eff 5-24-18; ss by #13650, eff 5-25-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-c6900.html"
}
